COMSOL MODEL PARAMETER AND BOUNDARY-CONDITION REGISTRY
======================================================

Repository location:
05_COMSOL_Model/

File:
COMSOL_Model_Parameter_and_Boundary_Condition_Registry.txt

Purpose
-------
This registry reconstructs the documented computational parameters,
constitutive assumptions, boundary conditions, gravity conditions,
numerical settings, primary outputs, and sensitivity specifications
for the patient-specific ventricular solid-mechanics model.

This registry is an evidence-control document. It distinguishes
documented model specifications from parameters for which actual
execution evidence has been recovered.

Evidence classes
----------------
CLASS 1 — SPECIFIED
The parameter or method is documented as part of the intended model.

CLASS 2 — EXECUTED
The parameter was used in an actual computational run and a corresponding
execution artifact is available.

CLASS 3 — VERIFIED
The executed parameter/model component has been checked against a
predefined numerical or methodological criterion.

CLASS 4 — MANUSCRIPT-REPORTED
The parameter/result has sufficient traceability to an underlying
execution artifact to support quantitative reporting.

NOT RECOVERED
The parameter is described in the reconstructed model documentation,
but the underlying numerical value or execution artifact has not yet
been recovered.

IMPORTANT CONTROL RULE
----------------------
A CLASS 1 specification must not be silently converted into a CLASS 2,
CLASS 3, or CLASS 4 claim.

Where an exact numerical parameter is not currently evidenced, the
manuscript should report the methodological formulation without
inventing a numerical value.

======================================================================
1. STUDY AND MODEL SCOPE
======================================================================

Study scope:
Patient-specific ventricular solid mechanics under gravity-dependent
loading.

Current documented pilot cohort:
P001–P005.

Input anatomy:
Patient-specific end-diastolic/end-systolic ventricular segmentation.

Primary computational framework:
Nonlinear finite-element solid mechanics.

Software:
COMSOL Multiphysics, version 6.4 listed in the recovered artifact
registry.

Primary mechanical endpoints:
1. Peak von Mises stress
2. Peak principal strain
3. Maximum ventricular displacement
4. LV cavity volume
5. Myocardial volume
6. Strain energy

Important scope restriction:
The recovered COMSOL documentation does NOT independently establish
execution of:
- CFD
- fluid–structure interaction (FSI)
- electrophysiology
- baroreflex control
- chronic remodeling
- pressure–volume-loop simulation
- astronaut-specific validation

These components must not be represented as executed components of the
present solid-mechanics model unless independent executable evidence is
recovered.

